Krita Nova 65 - Touch painting "automatic": remember that a pen was used

With Settings > Configure Krita > General > Tools > "Touch painting" on its
default, automatic, fingers paint until a pen input arrives - but only pen
input of the current session counted, so after every start of Krita a
finger painted on the canvas until the pen had been used once.

The first pen input is now remembered (kritarc novaPenInputSeen): from then
on, the automatic setting keeps fingers from painting right from the start.
Choosing "Enabled" or "Disabled" for touch painting works as before.

diff --git a/libs/ui/kis_config.cc b/libs/ui/kis_config.cc
index 9ed7604..ffe2f45 100644
--- a/libs/ui/kis_config.cc
+++ b/libs/ui/kis_config.cc
@@ -165,7 +165,21 @@ bool KisConfig::disableTouchOnCanvas() const
         // Automatic detection: enable or disable touch input based on whether
         // we've received a tablet input during this session and therefore know
         // that the user has a pen available.
-        return KoPointerEvent::tabletInputReceived();
+        //
+        // Krita Nova: ...or in an earlier session. Only this session counted,
+        // so after every start fingers painted until the pen was used once.
+        // The first pen input is remembered (kritarc novaPenInputSeen).
+        if (KoPointerEvent::tabletInputReceived()) {
+            static bool remembered = false;
+            if (!remembered) {
+                remembered = true;
+                if (!m_cfg.readEntry("novaPenInputSeen", false)) {
+                    KisConfig(false).writeEntry("novaPenInputSeen", true);
+                }
+            }
+            return true;
+        }
+        return m_cfg.readEntry("novaPenInputSeen", false);
     }
 }
 
